  "paragraphs": [
    "Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play.",
    "Maqam Bayati is by far one of the most popular and common maqamat in the Arabic repertory. It is also the main maqam in the Bayati Family. Its scale starts with Jins Bayati on the tonic followed by either Jins Nahawand or Jins Rast on the 4th degree.",
    "Maqam Muhayyar is a version of Maqam Bayati whose sayr starts at the octave note (called Muhayyar in the old Arabic scale). Maqam Muhayyar often uses Jins Rast on the 4th degree to ascend then emphasizes Jins Bayati on the octave before descending through the other ajnas common to Maqam Bayati.",
    "Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Bayati Family.",
    "Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Bayati by Sami Abu Shumays."
  ],
  "text": "Maqam Bayati The principal maqam in the Maqam Bayati Family Maqam Index Pronunciation of Bayati Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Bayati is by far one of the most popular and common maqamat in the Arabic repertory. It is also the main maqam in the Bayati Family. Its scale starts with Jins Bayati on the tonic followed by either Jins Nahawand or Jins Rast on the 4 th degree. Maqam Muhayyar is a version of Maqam Bayati whose sayr starts at the octave note (called Muhayyar in the old Arabic scale). Maqam Muhayyar often uses Jins Rast on the 4 th degree to ascend then emphasizes Jins Bayati on the octave before descending through the other ajnas common to Maqam Bayati. Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Bayati Family . Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Bayati by Sami Abu Shumays. ‘Ala Balad el-Mahbub Waddini (1935) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Akun Sa‘id (1932) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt) Lamma-nta Nawi (1929) Vocals and Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Mijana and ‘Ataba Wadih Al-Safi Music from Lebanese Folklore Muwashah Imlali al-Aqdaha Sirfan Sabah Fakhri (Traditional) Nura Nura (1953) Music and Vocals by Farid al-Atrash Ya Rayt Minnun (Qanun Taqsim) Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe Ya Rayt Minnun Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe Sama‘i Bayati Ibrahim al-‘Aryan Farhan Sabbagh (Oud solo) Sama‘i Bayati Iskandar Shalfun Ensemble Morkos",
